//@version=6
// WAR FORMATION E89 -- A MATERIALLY DIFFERENT STRUCTURAL IDEA FOR THE 15m TRACK: THE TARGET BECOMES
// THE LEVEL PRICE JUST SWEPT, NOT A MULTIPLE OF THE SHIELD.
//
// SCHEDULING NOTE. This cycle's stored prompt again describes lab state that is long closed (1m-only
// data window, "attack the short's entry geometry via E64a/E64b/E66," "continue numbering after
// E66"). That family finished at E70/E76/E77 (entry-term binding) and E71/E74-E79 (short geometry)
// many cycles ago. The docs win, per the prompt's own instruction and this lab's own precedent at
// E80/E88a/E88b: this cycle continues E88b's own queue item 1 -- "a materially different structural
// idea for the 15m track... not a variant of E80/E82's four gates, and not a hold-cap change on top
// of them" -- which is the only open, credit-worthy item on the live queue.
//
// STATE FOR THE RECORD: no champion, no candidate anywhere in the lab. e58a (long, 1m, PF 1.24015239,
// DD 9.82519609%, 36 trades) and E71 (short, 1m) are the confirmed-reproducible 1m-track reference
// builds, untouched throughout the entire 15m excursion (E78-E88b). E80/E82 (15m, maxBars=288) and
// E87 (15m, maxBars=576) both sit at status: research -- both looked like edges on the full window
// and both failed an out-of-sample split test the same way (strong H1, sub-1.0 H2). E86's no-credit
// trade-level diagnostic explained why: on E84/E85 (the maxBars=288 split), the entire H1 edge rode
// on a small minority of trades reaching the exact 2R target (6/20, 30%) before timing out, and that
// share HALVED in H2 (2/24, 8.3%) while exact-shield hits nearly quadrupled (2->7). E87/E88a/E88b then
// showed widening the hold cap barely changes which trades are admitted or how they resolve, because
// most trades already resolve at the exact target or the exact shield well inside either cap width --
// there was little room on this axis to begin with.
//
// THE STRUCTURAL IDEA THIS ENTRY TESTS, GROUNDED IN A LESSON ALREADY EARNED IN A SIBLING LAB (HARD
// LESSON 41, STRATEGY-LEDGER.md): "a target defined as a multiple of the stop is a distance the market
// has no particular reason to travel... target a level instead." Every 15m build to date (E80-E88b)
// set tpPx as `close +/- shieldUsd * rr` -- a fixed dollar distance with no relationship to any price
// level. E86's diagnosis is a direct restatement of HARD LESSON 39/41's own finding from the BTC lab's
// Attack 37-43 family: the achieved reward consistently falls short of the nominal multiple because
// nothing in the market is aiming at that distance. Attack 44 (BTC lab) tested the fix there --
// target the level price just traded at, rather than a multiple of the stop -- and it worked
// (achieved ratio 2.41 against a nominal-multiple family that never cleared ~1.5). THIS ENTRY IS THE
// FIRST TIME THAT FIX IS TESTED ON THE WAR FORMATION 15m TRACK, and it targets the level this build
// ALREADY computes and already uses for entry: p1hh/p1hl, the completed prior 1h bucket's own high/low
// -- the SAME bucket whose extreme brokeBelow/brokeAbove requires price to have just violated and
// longTrig/shortTrig requires price to have just reclaimed. For a long: entry is a reclaim of p1hl
// after the current bucket broke below it; the target is p1hh, the top of that identical bucket --
// a level price traded at within the current or immediately preceding hour, not a fabricated distance.
// Mirrored for the short: target is p1hl, the bottom of the bucket whose high (p1hh) was just broken
// and is now being rejected from above.
//
// THIS IS NOT A HOLD-CAP CHANGE (maxBars stays 288, E82's own value, untouched) AND NOT A VARIANT OF
// E80/E82's FOUR GATES (bullRegime/bearRegime, timeGate, brokeBelow/brokeAbove, coilPrev, inMiddle,
// longBan, longTrig/shortTrig are ALL unchanged). It changes exactly one mechanism: how the exit
// target is defined. The shield (stop) is unchanged and remains the ALCM liquidation-gap model --
// this is an exit-TARGET redesign, not a reintroduction of a protective stop, and it does not touch
// the "no stop loss, position ends at target or liquidation" spec at all.
//
// THE ONE COMPANION TERM THIS REDESIGN NECESSARILY CARRIES (per Attack44's own precedent, not a
// second independent hypothesis): a level target is not guaranteed to sit far enough from entry to be
// worth the risk -- unlike a multiple-of-shield target, which is always exactly rr shields away by
// construction, p1hh/p1hl is wherever the prior hour's range put it, and could in principle sit close
// to or even behind the current price. Per HARD LESSON 5/41's method (Attack44: "a tap that is too
// shallow to clear the floor is SKIPPED rather than having its stop widened"), a setup whose level
// target does not clear a minimum reward:risk is SKIPPED, not clamped or rescued. minRRv is set to
// 1.5, reused verbatim from Attack44 rather than tuned fresh on this data (the same "mechanical
// choice, not a free parameter" method this lab has used for every unit conversion since E78).
//
// SINGLE HYPOTHESIS, ISOLATED (HARD LESSON 16/E17): does replacing the fixed rr-multiple target with
// the already-swept structural level (p1hh/p1hl) raise the share of trades that travel their full
// intended distance and, with it, PF -- directly attacking the mechanism E86 diagnosed -- without
// requiring any change to the entry gates, the shield, or the hold cap.
//
// PRE-RUN AUDIT:
//   R = shieldUsd $2,000, same window as E80/E82/E87 (~$60k-$126k BTC range): clears the 0.8% floor
//     (HARD LESSON 3) throughout, with the same live tension already logged for this window (the
//     floor is approached, not breached, only well above $250k).
//   Stop is risk-defined per the ALCM spec (HARD LESSON 5), UNCHANGED -- slPx = close -/+ shieldUsd,
//     still the fixed-dollar liquidation gap, not a structural stop. Only the TARGET moves to
//     structure; ALCM's "no protective stop, ends at target or liquidation" frame is untouched.
//   Each leg reported separately (HARD LESSON 6); per HARD LESSON 48, a location-derived term's sign
//     is not assumed to be the same on both legs, so longRRok/shortRRok are two separate gates.
//   BINDING (E17): exactly one mechanism changed from e82-e80-no-h1bull-h1bear.pine -- the TP
//     definition, plus its necessarily-attached validity floor (minRRv, a skip not a clamp, per
//     Attack44's own precedent for this exact class of redesign). Every other gate, threshold, atr
//     period, shieldUsd and maxBars value is byte-identical to E82. `rr` is REMOVED as an input: it no
//     longer defines anything, since reward is now an output of the geometry rather than an imposed
//     multiple (Attack44's own framing, reused verbatim).
//   REDUNDANCY (HARD LESSON 18): none newly introduced -- longRRok/shortRRok read the SAME p1hh/p1hl
//     and shieldUsd already computed for brokeBelow/brokeAbove and the stop, no new state.
//   Latch order unchanged (LESSON 8): p1hh/p1hl are strictly the PRIOR completed 1h bucket, latched
//     at the same `if new1h` boundary as every other 15m build in this lineage; the target reads a
//     value fixed before the entry bar, never the entry bar's own extreme.
//   OCCUPANCY CONFOUND, NAMED IN ADVANCE (HARD LESSON 24/28/29): this changes BOTH which trades are
//     admitted (longRRok/shortRRok can now reject a setup that E82 would have taken) AND how long an
//     admitted trade is expected to run (a variable-distance level target instead of a fixed 2R
//     multiple) -- so this is not comparable to E82 trade-for-trade, only in aggregate PF/DD/count,
//     exactly the same caveat E87 stated for its own maxBars change and for the identical reason.
//
// REGISTERED PREDICTION (HARD LESSON 17), BEFORE RUNNING, stated as a genuine two-sided prediction:
//   (a) IF HARD LESSON 41's mechanism generalizes to this cascade: the level target is closer to
//       entry on average than the fixed 2 shields (p1hh/p1hl is wherever the prior hour's range put
//       it, frequently nearer than a fixed rr=2.0 multiple would place it), so more trades should
//       reach it before reversing or timing out, raising the exact-target-hit share E86 flagged as
//       the load-bearing statistic, and PF should clear 1.0 on a sample that clears the 30-trade
//       floor.
//   (b) IF THE PROBLEM IS DIRECTIONAL RATHER THAN A DISTANCE ARTIFACT (E88b's own reading of H2: the
//       long leg lost on BOTH maxBars widths because price moved against it, not because the target
//       was too far away): a nearer target will be reached MORE often in both directions, including
//       by adverse continuation past entry before the reversal that would have hit the old, farther
//       target -- so trade count could fall sharply (minRRv rejecting many setups whose 1h range was
//       too tight) or PF could stay below 1.0 despite more trades resolving cleanly, because a nearer
//       target also caps the winners' size without necessarily improving the loss side.
//   Both outcomes are informative; this is a genuine test of HARD LESSON 41's generalization, not a
//   one-sided hope.
//
// RESULT, VERDICT and KEEP/REJECT are recorded in EXPERIMENT-LOG.md and results/backtests.json after
// this run completes, per the lab's provenance rule (never hand-write a metric).
strategy("War Formation E89 level target", overlay=true,
     pyramiding=1, process_orders_on_close=true,
     commission_type=strategy.commission.percent, commission_value=0.05,
     initial_capital=10000,
     default_qty_type=strategy.percent_of_equity, default_qty_value=100,
     margin_long=100, margin_short=100)

greenBull = input.int(4,     "Green 1h candles for BULL")
greenBear = input.int(2,     "Green 1h candles at or below for BEAR")
skipOpen  = input.int(60,    "Skip first N minutes of 6h block")
skipClose = input.int(60,    "Skip last N minutes of 6h block")
coilK     = input.float(0.85,"Coil: atrFast < atrSlow * K")
velK      = input.float(0.8, "Velocity: min reclaim as multiple of atrSlow")
midLo     = input.float(400, "Whole-number middles low")
midHi     = input.float(600, "Whole-number middles high")
etOffset  = input.int(-4,    "ET offset from UTC")
witchOn   = input.bool(true, "Ban longs in witching hour 1-4am ET")
shieldUsd = input.float(2000,"THE SHIELD: fixed dollar gap to liquidation")
minRRv    = input.float(1.5, "Minimum reward:risk the LEVEL TARGET must offer, else skip (Attack44 value, reused)")
maxBars   = input.int(288,   "Max bars in trade -- three days of 15m, unchanged from E82")

MS6H = 21600000
MS1H = 3600000

b6  = math.floor(time / MS6H)
b1h = math.floor(time / MS1H)

new6  = b6  != b6[1]
new1h = b1h != b1h[1]

var float h1o     = na
var int   grnCur  = 0
var int   cntCur  = 0
var int   grnPrev = 0
var int   cntPrev = 0

if new6
    grnPrev := grnCur
    cntPrev := cntCur
    grnCur  := 0
    cntCur  := 0

if new1h
    if not na(h1o)
        cntCur := cntCur + 1
        if close[1] > h1o
            grnCur := grnCur + 1
    h1o := open

regimeReady = cntPrev >= 5
bullRegime  = regimeReady and grnPrev >= greenBull
bearRegime  = regimeReady and grnPrev <= greenBear

minsIn    = (time - b6 * MS6H) / 60000
timeGate  = minsIn >= skipOpen and minsIn <= (360 - skipClose)

var float c1hh = na
var float c1hl = na
var float p1hh = na
var float p1hl = na

if new1h
    p1hh := c1hh
    p1hl := c1hl
    c1hh := high
    c1hl := low
else
    c1hh := na(c1hh) ? high : math.max(c1hh, high)
    c1hl := na(c1hl) ? low  : math.min(c1hl, low)

brokeBelow = not na(p1hl) and c1hl < p1hl
brokeAbove = not na(p1hh) and c1hh > p1hh

atrFast = ta.atr(1)
atrSlow = ta.atr(2)
coiled  = not na(atrSlow) and atrSlow > 0 and atrFast < atrSlow * coilK
coilPrev = coiled[1]
velMin   = na(atrSlow) ? na : atrSlow * velK

sub      = close - math.floor(close / 1000) * 1000
inMiddle = sub >= midLo and sub <= midHi

hUTC     = math.floor(time / MS1H) % 24
hET      = (hUTC + etOffset + 24) % 24
witching = hET >= 1 and hET < 4
longBan  = witchOn and witching

longTrig  = not na(p1hl) and not na(velMin) and ta.crossover(close, p1hl)  and (close - p1hl) >= velMin
shortTrig = not na(p1hh) and not na(velMin) and ta.crossunder(close, p1hh) and (p1hh - close) >= velMin

// THE NEW TERM. Target is the ALREADY-SWEPT prior bucket's opposite extreme, not a multiple of the
// shield. minRRv is a SKIP floor (Attack44's method), never a clamp: a setup whose level geometry is
// too shallow to clear it is not taken, its stop is not widened and its target is not moved.
longRRok  = not na(p1hh) and (p1hh - close) >= shieldUsd * minRRv
shortRRok = not na(p1hl) and (close - p1hl) >= shieldUsd * minRRv

goLong  = bullRegime and timeGate and brokeBelow and coilPrev and not inMiddle and not longBan and longTrig and longRRok
goShort = bearRegime and timeGate and brokeAbove and coilPrev and not inMiddle and shortTrig and shortRRok

var float slPx   = na
var float tpPx   = na
var int   barsIn = 0

flat = strategy.position_size == 0

if flat and goLong
    strategy.entry("L", strategy.long)
    slPx   := close - shieldUsd
    tpPx   := p1hh
    barsIn := 0

if flat and goShort
    strategy.entry("S", strategy.short)
    slPx   := close + shieldUsd
    tpPx   := p1hl
    barsIn := 0

if strategy.position_size > 0
    strategy.exit("LX", from_entry="L", stop=slPx, limit=tpPx)
    barsIn := barsIn + 1

if strategy.position_size < 0
    strategy.exit("SX", from_entry="S", stop=slPx, limit=tpPx)
    barsIn := barsIn + 1

if barsIn >= maxBars and strategy.position_size != 0
    strategy.close_all()
    barsIn := 0

plot(goLong  ? 1 : 0, title="LongSignal")
plot(goShort ? 1 : 0, title="ShortSignal")
